The test has three phases. In `lib/matplotlib/scale.py`, the forward log implementation is `LogTransform.transform_non_affine`, while the inverted log uses a different `transform_non_affine` method on `InvertedLogTransform`, and symlog uses `SymmetricalLogTransform.transform_non_affine`, so only calls to the forward `LogTransform` method count. The first phase stays on linear scales, so it contributes none; the third phase sets `symlog` on y, so it also contributes none. In the middle log-log phase, both `set_xscale("log")` and `set_yscale("log")` create `LogScale` objects whose `get_transform()` returns a `LogTransform`, and the counted forward-log method is invoked three times during that phase in total.

